<newsitem itemid="192432" id="root" date="1996-11-15" xml:lang="en">
<title>HONG KONG: S. Megga year net returns to profit.</title>
<headline>S. Megga year net returns to profit.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-11-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended June 30</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	  0.31 gain   vs 2.87 loss</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)   nil	   vs nil</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	 23.91 gain  vs nil</p>
<p>    Net			   1.80 profit vs 16.41 loss</p>
<p>    Turnover		    871.02	vs 882.24</p>
<p>    Company name		S. Megga International Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		 December 18-24</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	  N/A</p>
<p>NOTE - S. Megga International makes telecommunications products, including cordless and feature telephones, and facsimile machines.</p>
<p>The exceptional item is a capital profit arising from the repurchase and subsequent cancellation of the company's convertible notes after deducting the related expenses.</p>
<p>Total dividend for the year is nil vs two H.K. cents.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
</text>
